{
  "item": "DarkSkull01",
  "mu_name": "Dark Skull Soldier",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain _enum.h MONSTER_DARK_SKULL_SOLDIER_1 (86), drawn as MODEL_DARK_SKULL_SOLDIER = MODEL_MONSTER01 + 59, so OpenMonsterModel loads Monster60.bmd; the client's name is 흑해골전사, 'black skull warrior' (ZzzCharacter.cpp:13482). WebZen's Monster.txt:114 calls breed 86 'Elite Orc'; MuMain's English client and OpenMU S6 BloodCastle1.cs call it Dark Skull Soldier. docs/blood-castle-port.md Part B 3.",
  "world": "bloodcastle",
  "object_type": 86,
  "monster": {
    "model_index": 59,
    "scale": 1.0
  },
  "monster_from": "ZzzCharacter.cpp:13468-13483, CreateMonster, case MONSTER_DARK_SKULL_SOLDIER_1..8: OpenMonsterModel(MONSTER_MODEL_DARK_SKULL_SOLDIER); CreateCharacter(Key, MODEL_DARK_SKULL_SOLDIER, ...); Weapon[0] and Weapon[1] = MODEL_CRESCENT_AXE at Level 0; Scale = 1.0f. No BlendMesh, no effect.",
  "right_hand": "Axe09",
  "right_hand_bone": "attack02",
  "left_hand": "Axe09",
  "left_hand_bone": "attack01",
  "right_hand_from": "MODEL_CRESCENT_AXE is Item/Axe09.bmd (cooked, the Cyclops's). Weapon[0] in right_hand, as the Cyclops's; its bone is CreateCharacter's weapon switch, case MODEL_DARK_SKULL_SOLDIER: Weapon[0].LinkBone = 33, Weapon[1].LinkBone = 20 (ZzzCharacter.cpp:11950-11953) -- attack02 and attack01 in this rig.",
  "profile": "monster",
  "rig_from": "Eight actions, exported with --actions=all. 57 bones, a biped with weapon bones attack01 (20) and attack02 (33).",
  "sheets": {
    "npc_b1": "darkskull_npc_b1.png",
    "bons": "bons.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Two sheets, .OZJ with no alpha: Data/Monster/npc_b1 (128x128, the armour, 654 triangles), decoded as darkskull_npc_b1; and bons (128x128, the bare skull and bones, 56), byte for byte the Skeleton's bons.png and shared with it.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "npc_b1": "plate_steel",
    "bons": "bone"
  },
  "sheet_materials_from": "Read off the sheets at 2x: npc_b1 is black lacquered plate with red flame-shaped trim on every piece -- painted_steel, as the Blood Castle orcs', grain taken out; bons the skull and bones, bone as the Skeleton's. Then plate_steel, 2026-10-03 (the user: 'skeleton warion metal armors doont look realistical enoguht also they are pretty light'; of Orc01 first, 'its better'): a real metal, half its reflectance taken from the painting, so the plate goes dark steel in its shadows and catches the moon and the lamps on its edges instead of reading as painted plastic; the grain override kept on it.",
  "material_overrides": {
    "plate_steel": {
      "grain": {
        "depth": 0.01,
        "roughness_range": 0.01
      }
    }
  },
  "material_overrides_why": "As Orc01's: painted_steel's brushed grain striped the plate (the user: 'kind fo striped?'), so it is all but taken out.",
  "sounds_from": "ZzzOpenData.cpp:3802-3808: mBullDie, mHunter2, mBlackSkullDie and mBlackSkullAttack, SetMonsterSound(..., 188, -1, 190, -1, 189) -- offsets from SOUND_MONSTER_BULL1 = 210: 398 HUNTER2_ to walk, 400 BLACKSKULLATTACK to swing and flinch, 399 BLACKSKULLDIE to die (DSPlaySound.h:339-341). Wired as darkskullsoldier_* in sounds.json.",
  "islands_from": "23 islands for 710 triangles. Island 0 (56, u 0.45-0.72, v 0.40-0.71) is the whole of the bons group in the .obj -- the bare skull -- bone; the other 22 are npc_b1's armour, painted_steel. They arrived as skin, the monster profile's default.",
